<description>&lt;p&gt;Venezuela disclosed a $237.5 billion debt pile and moved forward with a large restructuring while the United States signed a security cooperation pact with the interim Venezuelan government, after which a U.S. marine died falling overboard during a Caribbean operation linked to the renewed ties. The Senate is probing JD Vance for allegedly steering a Venezuelan oil license to Vitol and another senator’s role in the same deal, while Citi weighs a market re-entry after a five-year exit. Venezuelan authorities later declared the security pact null and void, illegal gold mining continues, and Eni and Repsol pledged a $2 billion joint-venture investment. According to UCDP, there were 2 battle-related deaths in 2007.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Machine-written from the linked sources, checked for figures and names not in them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiSEFVX3lxTE05RUgxMXB2Qm9ia3NEQi05a1V3bG4tbmxscjh5Q1hQc242YXhaSVg0RldkYlRpcEJNdlhTLWI4Zm1qNnBZNjNzYQ?oc=5&quot;&gt;Dawn&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMivwFBVV95cUxNSnBhS2YxRk5nTjRFbDJON0ROb19SVEYzc2dGYUpnb0ozdzV0Y2p2eHRjMVlYd3p3M09lam1qTHN2dkNhVDhsZmVvNUE3NXg3dFlCOWh4NUNzVXNqUmt4LVBDRFNCdDNGdlU0ak9hVTY1c1J4VXJ4a2stZndwbzE3b2QxLWxjMlJydmNkUlJDTTRDTmdDV21PS2hraVRUT0pLM29OLXJtZV9kaVhqTWlRc2tWM25tMFdNUnR0RXU3TQ?oc=5&quot;&gt;Reuters&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiwAFBVV95cUxOakxRRS1xODNKVEMzdlowcjUzd2g4amNoV0JSSzdQc0JEUXg1WWxSbGxOaGhYWDZWSlQzeldBelpvUnpXb3g3bHdMUWd4NWhiZFJRZnEtSWU4TDBXS0Q1Q21CWE9QUkxkT2YxYVI5MzlJNkVJS3FRZ3NuMG90Y0JBMFNKRGEtOEhlOUktTVJwU2hoSHVVVW56NXI0ZlZIOHo3TGt0UTc3VnA4VlV5MGZoTmlfS05qQlpQcWpiUWNtSjI?oc=5&quot;&gt;Reuters&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;NewsBreak: Local News &amp;amp; Alerts&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMimgFBVV95cUxPcnB4MUZDQ0pGMjJPWERzTXg0LU83YlJ6N3pUNHN6UTNHV1NjS2FGWThZ